	(footprint "pluto_cal_switch:TSNP-6_0.7x1.1_P0.4_NSMD"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "39e44b1f-93f3-4e15-98b1-ecee21a5e022")
		(at 50.65 64.45 90)
		(descr "Infineon PG-TSNP-6 (0.7 x 1.1 x 0.37 mm leadless, 0.40 mm pitch both axes) - BGS12WN6 C534203, and the pin-, truth-table- and LAND-identical BGS12P2L6 C3312945. Land from BGS12WN6 Rev 2.9 Figure 5 'Footprint recommendation': NSMD, six 0.25x0.25 mm lands on a 0.40x0.40 mm grid, a SINGLE solder-mask opening over all six (the 0.15 mm land-to-land gap is below JLCPCB's 0.2 mm mask-dam minimum, so per-pad openings are unmanufacturable), and 6 circular D0.25 stencil apertures. Pin map from Figure 2 (TOP VIEW): left col 4/5/6, right col 3/2/1. PIN-2 GROUND VIA MUST ESCAPE OUTWARD (ARCHITECTURE sec.10.7): a 0.45 mm standard-tier via at the 0.25 mm land leaves 0.050 mm to pins 1 and 3, under the 0.127 mm floor - this part is why the board is jlc_4layer_advanced (0.25/0.15 vias fit, 0.150 mm clear).")
		(tags "TSNP-6 PG-TSNP-6-10 DFN RF SPDT Infineon BGS12WN6 BGS12P2L6 NSMD")
