		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "6e5f7a0f-48f5-45ae-ab1b-92422638509c")
		(at 30.25 45.75)
		(descr "SMA jack, vertical THT square flange, 5-D1.4 mm holes on a 5.08x5.08 mm square (Kinghelm KH-SMA-KE-Z / C504007, drawing sheet 2-2 'PCB layout'; depth reserve BWSMA-KE-Z001 / C496549 on the identical pattern). Drills are D1.4 NOT the KiCad Wurth pattern's 1.5/1.7 - ADR-0007: a 0.9 mm square post has a 1.273 mm diagonal, so D1.3 leaves 0.014 mm and D1.4 leaves 0.064 mm. Pad 1 carries a 0.75 mm local clearance = the >=D3.5 mm bottom-plane antipad (ADR-0007 RULE 1, ~9 dB of return loss at 6 GHz over the D2.6 minimum-DRC opening); pads 2-5 carry none so the top pour stays continuous to the ground posts (RULE 4).")
