	(footprint "pluto_cal_switch:MCLP-6-EP_2x2_P0.65_MC1630"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "9ed0d854-7f46-4a44-89c1-00bda7de6995")
		(at 81.94 55 90)
		(descr "Mini-Circuits MCLP 2x2 mm leadless, case style MC1630 (YAT-xA+ fixed attenuator family: YAT-10A+ C5839318, YAT-2A+ C5205333 - one land qualifies the whole family). Land MEASURED off the YAT-10A+ REV B p.3 SUGGESTED PCB LAYOUT (PL-586) drawing, calibrated on that drawing's own 2.00x2.00 mm dashed PACKAGE OUTLINE: 6 lands 0.30x0.80 mm at 0.65 mm pitch, rows at y=+/-0.937, EP land 1.25x0.65 mm. Pin numbering from p.2 TOP VIEW (bottom row 1,2,3 L-R; top row 6,5,4; index over pin 1). PAD 7 (EP) IS THE RF GROUND RETURN, NOT A THERMAL PAD ('Case is defined as ground lead', abs-max note 3) - it must NOT be tented, and it carries NO in-pad vias: PL-586's 31x D0.2 epoxy-plugged PTH are geometrically impossible at JLC on a 0.30 mm land, so ground vias go OUTSIDE the lands in the surrounding pour (declared deviation, part.yaml layout.notes).")
