	(footprint "pluto_cal_switch:SW_Push_1P1T_XKB_TS-1187A"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "ac46cf6d-a94f-4ea0-9cc7-2d9e0d2a5f12")
		(at 95 30)
		(descr "SPST-NO momentary tact switch, XKB TS-1187A-B-A-B (C318884), SMD-4P gull-wing, 5.1 x 5.1 x 1.5 mm. DECLARED-PARTIAL LAND: XKB publishes no datasheet PDF and no recommended land for this SKU (LCSC C318884 re-read 2026-07-28), so the pads are deliberately oversized to 1.60 x 1.20 at (+/-2.80, +/-1.75) to tolerate +/-0.4 mm of lead-position error; jlc_twin PAD-GEOM at stage 7 is the gate that closes it. Pads 1-2 are one contact, 3-4 the other (standard 4-pad tact arrangement, asserted not quoted) - benign here because 1/2 carry USB_BOOT and 3/4 carry GND, so any wrong pairing fails LOUDLY at first power-up.")
